; The least-primitives doctrine, measured. Eight digits, low to high: a derived op
; equals its hand-written native expansion (same tree); that holds for every
; O(1)-derivable comparison and boolean; so derivation is compile-time lowering to
; native nodes, not runtime dispatch -- free; mul-from-add is correct (3*100=300);
; but it is O(b), depth tracking b (2*100=200); so mul stays primitive because an
; asymptotically-worse derivation is not free -- the boundary between push-to-rewrite
; and keep-native; the comparison floor is two (eq, lt); and le sits one over it,
; derivable as (if (lt b a) 0 1).
import "../primitive-minimality.fk"
